Label DRM nodes and the files that identify this laptop's GPU with existing graphics types:
the device files Google labels sysfs_gpu for its own GPU at 00:02.0. libdrm reads uevent,
vendor, device and subsystem IDs to list a GPU; without them Mesa finds no DRM device and
SurfaceFlinger aborts in a loop. No permissions or domains change.
Drop the PCI-path entry when Google's labels cover it.

--- a/etc/selinux/vendor_file_contexts
+++ b/etc/selinux/vendor_file_contexts
@@ -389,3 +389,6 @@
 /vendor/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.boot@1\.2-service\.android-desktop u:object_r:hal_bootctl_default_exec:s0
 /vendor/bin/hw/vendor\.dolby\.media\.c2-default-service-dax-desktop            u:object_r:mediacodec_exec:s0
 /vendor/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.graphics\.allocator-service\.minigbm   u:object_r:hal_graphics_allocator_default_exec:s0
+/dev/dri/card[0-9]+ u:object_r:gpu_device:s0
+/dev/dri/renderD[0-9]+ u:object_r:gpu_device:s0
+/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:08\.1/0000:03:00\.0/(uevent|vendor|device|subsystem_vendor|subsystem_device|revision|config|resource|irq) u:object_r:sysfs_gpu:s0
